#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486367 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486351 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdab7649-2d4d-5516-bf04-cfe674bbd3f8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Additive Inverse"}] :question/id #uuid "2ce7e093-c668-5ab6-b343-b49f04300b13" :question/math-academy-id "e-22712" :question/problem "How can we represent the additive inverse of $-2$ on the number line?" :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of a number is the number that lies at the same distance from zero on the number line, but on the opposite side. \n\nAs we can see on the number line below, the distance of $-2$ from zero is $2$ units. The only other number that is at a distance of $2$ units from zero is $2.$\n\n![](images/03/035ad7581b3084ab33917ceb4560b46054871f96551b30825d5c14239a7c0687.png)\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of $-2$ is $2$, and it can be represented on the number line as follows:\n\n![](images/75/75b5ed5f417e89d2ed58f5b2892f43bdbf64ca44da2e7b031a18a9147fd2940a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486432 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486349 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "056c4886-b3e9-575a-b584-1840a577d04e" :knowledge-point/title "Adding Opposite Quantities"}] :question/id #uuid "b716c849-40fa-5f39-a344-ee1a0ebde20d" :question/math-academy-id "e-22721" :question/problem "A drone’s elevation **dropped by** $85\\text{ m}$ while descending into a valley. Then it **rose by** $85\\text{ m}$ while flying back up.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The drone’s elevation is now higher than the initial elevation.\n\nII. The drone’s elevation is now lower than the initial elevation.\n\nIII. The drone returned to the initial elevation." :question/worked-solution "In our situation:\n\n- While descending, the drone’s elevation *dropped by* $85\\text{ m}$, which is a change of $-85\\text{ m}.$\n\n- While climbing back up, the drone’s elevation *rose by* $85\\text{ m},$ which is a change of $+85\\text{ m}.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0{:}$\n\n$$\n-85 + 85 = 0\n$$\n\nThis means the *total elevation change* is $0\\text{ m},$ so the drone returns to the original elevation.\n\nSo, statements I and II are false, while statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486449 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486350 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Addition Using Absolute Value"}] :question/id #uuid "d5c1d845-4926-5b71-9aaf-b7f1a7983af3" :question/math-academy-id "e-22722" :question/problem "Let $p=-3$ and $q=8.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $p+q?$" :question/worked-solution "The value of $p+q$ is the number located a distance $|q|$ from $p$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $q$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $q$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $p = -3$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $q = 8$, so the distance we move is $|q| = 8.$\n\n- Because $q$ is *positive*, we move $8$ units to the *right* from $-3.$\n\n![](images/b4/b44a40ef3278f0b31899b7a98695a92e332859b5d0f7badb82a241b1bcbef022.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n-3 + 8 = 5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486349 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "056c4886-b3e9-575a-b584-1840a577d04e" :knowledge-point/title "Adding Opposite Quantities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84cfb290-8ccd-590d-aa27-4683d7aaed7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485996} {:answer/id #uuid "9c413feb-3e7c-58c3-ad79-38bc3137398f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-$20$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486044} {:answer/id #uuid "b037c639-2022-5ee4-afbe-0e75ebb6c03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$20$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486080} {:answer/id #uuid "c0acb70e-83fd-51d9-983c-cbded421e64c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-$40$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486110} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f63688-9724-5079-be15-ff720f739366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$40$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84cfb290-8ccd-590d-aa27-4683d7aaed7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485996} :answer-field/id #uuid "6460d5a3-b5e1-57f8-bcd3-5b782affce54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae45fb99-3296-59e3-8a59-381f72003cfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-356966" :question/problem "A bank account had an **initial balance** of $$0.$ During the day, there was a **deposit** of $$20.$ Then there was a **withdrawal** of $$20$ later.\nWhat is the resulting amount in the account?" :question/worked-solution "In our situation:\n\n- During the day, the account had a *deposit of* $$20,$ which is a change of $+$20.$\n\n- Later, the account had a *withdrawal of* $$20,$ which is a change of $-$20.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0:$\n\n$$\n20+(-20)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the balance returns to its original value of $$0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486350 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Addition Using Absolute Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122f3eb5-2bd7-59a3-826b-79b8d14830c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $3$ located $8$ units to the right of $-5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485797} {:answer/id #uuid "afc28c25-c38a-52de-999c-9758ec38dd31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $3$ located $5$ units to the right of $8.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486079} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f015b4-a229-5c1c-8fb0-f5f7cea2c939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $3$ located $8$ units to the left of $-5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486086} {:answer/id #uuid "ca24ff1b-a0e4-5917-85b7-7f99552c72ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-3$ located $8$ units to the left of $-5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486130} {:answer/id #uuid "db7931af-c972-55c9-92aa-6d922aa80776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-3$ located $8$ units to the right of $-5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "122f3eb5-2bd7-59a3-826b-79b8d14830c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $3$ located $8$ units to the right of $-5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485797} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b678d2a-3f69-50d5-841e-afd7ff418930" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fe75ee40-dd66-5b6a-be0b-41d26c4e980f" :question/math-academy-id "q-356982" :question/problem "Let $x=-5$ and $y=8.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $x+y?$" :question/worked-solution "The value of $x+y$ is the number located a distance $|y|$ from $x$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $y$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $y$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $x=-5$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $y=8$, so the distance we move is $|y|=8.$\n\n- Because $y$ is *positive*, we move $8$ units to the *right* from $-5.$\n\n![](images/6f/6f3852a3695e81aa36441b6e579cce31c337aa81aa5af8ee2944bdcce7fb76d3.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n-5+8=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486350 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Addition Using Absolute Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1618c5c4-03ee-55c3-8b45-973252793ff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $5$ located $9$ units to the left of $4.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485803} {:answer/id #uuid "3a49ffd0-69f7-5e09-bdfb-755e2f1ce19d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-5$ located $9$ units to the right of $4.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485879} {:answer/id #uuid "3a7ef876-0c99-59d3-ab8b-3570c64020e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $5$ located $9$ units to the right of $4.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485880} {:answer/id #uuid "7878abb2-a11b-59c9-9bae-7e232650f3ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-5$ located $4$ units to the right of $9.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485976} {:answer/id #uuid "fe39958e-4d16-547a-b78d-9abaafc84aa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-5$ located $9$ units to the left of $4.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe39958e-4d16-547a-b78d-9abaafc84aa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-5$ located $9$ units to the left of $4.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486229} :answer-field/id #uuid "06e00fbc-e98b-51ea-9bd5-55bb5ceb760f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5daaab8a-c401-527b-849d-4cd75e79ca94" :question/math-academy-id "q-356985" :question/problem "Let $u=4$ and $v=-9.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $u+v?$" :question/worked-solution "The value of $u+v$ is the number located a distance $|v|$ from $u$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $v$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $v$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $u=4$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $v=-9$, so the distance we move is $|v|=9.$\n\n- Because $v$ is *negative*, we move $9$ units to the *left* from $4.$\n\n![](images/79/79c5200c6f0089f7b6cf6be0eec8b97de3ff3a3daa270bfa6e7ae0c480b134f5.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n4+(-9)=-5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486349 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "056c4886-b3e9-575a-b584-1840a577d04e" :knowledge-point/title "Adding Opposite Quantities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a240731-37c3-544a-8985-4c388b8dd124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485839} {:answer/id #uuid "3faeae4d-7a22-58a6-9532-93cf78868277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485886} {:answer/id #uuid "8925d033-ba54-59a9-9aca-dcf29388620c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486008} {:answer/id #uuid "cc60c973-4861-5ee3-96d6-e6ef18377082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486134} {:answer/id #uuid "dcdef934-a585-5434-8be6-9e95072f0b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc60c973-4861-5ee3-96d6-e6ef18377082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486134} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f4683f9-9c21-5e8a-bbee-d3ba5dd3dafe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486294}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef66e122-a2b4-5616-86af-6621c724508e" :question/math-academy-id "q-356997" :question/problem "A drone’s elevation **rose by** $85\\text{ m}$ while flying up to a roof. Then it **dropped by** $85\\text{ m}$ while descending back to the pilot.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The drone's elevation is now higher than the initial elevation.\n\nII. The drone returned to the initial elevation.\n\nIII. The drone's elevation is now lower than the initial elevation." :question/worked-solution "In our situation:\n\n- While flying up to a roof, the drone’s elevation *rose by* $85\\text{ m}$, which is a change of $+85\\text{ m}.$\n\n- While descending back to the pilot, the drone’s elevation *dropped by* $85\\text{ m},$ which is a change of $-85\\text{ m}.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0:$\n\n$$\n85+(-85)=0\n$$\n\nThis means the *total elevation change* is $0\\text{ m},$ so the drone returns to the original elevation.\n\nSo, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486350 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Addition Using Absolute Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07472916-38b0-59bb-a457-2a4fc33c51b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-3$ located $9$ units to the right of $-6.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485780} {:answer/id #uuid "37e293ca-fd34-56bb-a2d5-33687c3d5855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $3$ located $9$ units to the right of $-6.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485871} {:answer/id #uuid "7a03d7b9-f033-5945-a9a4-7e8b1c0ae329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-3$ located $9$ units to the left of $-6.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485980} {:answer/id #uuid "92a6ef2e-c855-5d1e-a6f6-b70161e7c037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $3$ located $9$ units to the left of $-6.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486028} {:answer/id #uuid "f4f51ac5-69d4-5a8a-9881-b8eba317c491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $3$ located $6$ units to the right of $9.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37e293ca-fd34-56bb-a2d5-33687c3d5855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $3$ located $9$ units to the right of $-6.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485871} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfc83496-ab8e-51f7-b8d9-81dec906fb5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e975e85-092f-5a1a-be8e-b7301eb722e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-357007" :question/problem "Let $p=-6$ and $q=9.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $p+q?$" :question/worked-solution "The value of $p+q$ is the number located a distance $|q|$ from $p$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $q$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $q$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $p=-6$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $q=9$, so the distance we move is $|q|=9.$\n\n- Because $q$ is *positive*, we move $9$ units to the *right* from $-6.$\n\n![](images/17/17c56561e34f16a80df8ee8872401f7a3df4930c28c38ce70c1dcf202269f3d0.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n-6+9=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486429 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486350 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcbb661f-40e5-5926-8387-8720b43e57de" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Addition Using Absolute Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08e9e8c9-31a0-5e60-b977-a4bce4aacf19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-5$ located $1$ unit to the right of $6.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485784} {:answer/id #uuid "49c8390b-831a-5e22-9a5a-aa8232f54972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-5$ located $6$ units to the left of $1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485899} {:answer/id #uuid "5acd367d-d857-54b8-af86-04191b89d45c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-5$ located $6$ units to the right of $1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485923} {:answer/id #uuid "79bc2c29-b9c8-50a5-b4eb-12efd2b0d95f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $5$ located $6$ units to the left of $1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485979} {:answer/id #uuid "d0e280b8-2b2c-5df9-a631-0adc13f36f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $5$ located $6$ units to the right of $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49c8390b-831a-5e22-9a5a-aa8232f54972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It's the number $-5$ located $6$ units to the left of $1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485899} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe3dc164-1594-57e4-92cf-6547e4c7625a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2201c29-9c53-5378-91b2-19915c1b3e60" :question/math-academy-id "q-357009" :question/problem "Let $p=1$ and $q=-6.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $p+q?$" :question/worked-solution "The value of $p+q$ is the number located a distance $|q|$ from $p$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $q$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $q$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $p=1$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $q=-6$, so the distance we move is $|q|=6.$\n\n- Because $q$ is *negative*, we move $6$ units to the *left* from $1.$\n\n![](images/f4/f488d1dc3787fefc588e143e7808fee7e4473a9918986b49bc36344e6a153b25.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n1+(-6)=-5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486349 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "056c4886-b3e9-575a-b584-1840a577d04e" :knowledge-point/title "Adding Opposite Quantities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09d05043-ffb9-54b3-b4cb-eadb56501804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485786} {:answer/id #uuid "17f35cba-c71a-5ad7-833b-9439eb84c575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485809} {:answer/id #uuid "75746c38-5356-5b1d-a3d3-cc7b4ea5c6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485967} {:answer/id #uuid "9407b62d-ffa5-58a3-8579-5716cb7de206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486031} {:answer/id #uuid "b6641b91-f000-597b-96aa-8b3e773ca1d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6641b91-f000-597b-96aa-8b3e773ca1d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486091} :answer-field/id #uuid "b10fe7e3-ee29-5950-b544-d1a41e9a2d44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486313}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "caba3d37-19c8-51f8-9627-60834d1806c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-357097" :question/problem "The temperature inside an oven **dropped by** ${25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ when the door was opened. Then it **rose by** ${25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ when the door was closed.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The temperature is now lower than the initial value.\n\nII. The temperature returned to the initial value.\n\nIII. The temperature is now larger than the initial value." :question/worked-solution "In our situation:\n\n- When the door was opened, the temperature *dropped by* ${25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$, which is a change of $-{25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$\n\n- When the door was closed, the temperature *rose by* ${25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C},$ which is a change of $+{25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0:$\n\n$$\n-25+25=0\n$$\n\nThis means the *total temperature change* is ${0}^{∘}\\,\\text{C},$ so the temperature returns to its original value.\n\nSo, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486351 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdab7649-2d4d-5516-bf04-cfe674bbd3f8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Additive Inverse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3513abbb-1f4f-5bbb-b140-978f5e391ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/4986262570b7133149b8b709c64127873d5c1a90ef642c45e7b97850808dfb82.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485865} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb1fd9e-9548-5d3c-8ab9-c14c461e2865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/db/dbc14e9c10474229a888d11cae45af45519795913311118bd2532b52a72d7ddb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485956} {:answer/id #uuid "aa3b2e55-72db-55f9-97f9-7bba3eb17290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3d/3dfb8c3d3e94af3cef8233628aa3e640766cf5a2f8e282426dfed15acc58f2a1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486072} {:answer/id #uuid "df97d783-8afb-58b6-9fda-1d6b3c262e2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f66b9ac4ab46cbf1498e5f71092b34e25dc26649b36af65cf86cdc5ac0c25cc6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486173} {:answer/id #uuid "f834df38-49ba-59f3-a58e-9d3780e5c719" :answer/type {: